<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S5.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LLaMA-7B at 20% sparsity.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effect of different training tokens on perplexity and zero-shot mean accuracy on different models.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.3.4 </span>Datasets</h4>

<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="S5.T6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Dataset ablation at 20% sparsity.<span id="S5.T6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We report the change in WikiText-2 perplexity and zero-shot mean accuracy relative to training masks on our default dataset (FineWeb-Edu) for LLaMA-7B and DeepSeekMoE-16B. Negative <math id="S5.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>PPL and positive <math id="S5.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>Acc indicate improvement.</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T6.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:165.6pt;height:29.2pt;vertical-align:-13.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-57.6pt,10.2pt) scale(0.589623629441322,0.589623629441322) ;">
